从安保和监控场景起步，既有人形也有非人形机器人产品，其控制策略设计更加强调安全性和稳定性；文章给出通用具身智能架构：视觉和语言模型联合用于感知与任务理解，行为规 
划模块负责编制行动计划，低层通过强化学习和模仿学习控制实现执行，从而形成闭环；文章称 Figure、1X                                                                  
等代表公司在过去三到五年里完成多轮融资，金额集中的高位显示资本集中度很高；文章指出具身智能创始团队多源自动驾驶、大模型和传统机器人企业，具备跨领域背景。[18]     

现有公开资料显示：CSDN 文章解释模仿学习路径：通过人类示教和演示数据训练机器人，让其学习动作模式；CSDN                                                            
文章解释强化学习路径：机器人在仿真或现实环境中通过奖励信号和试错优化策略，实现任务目标；文章指出在具身智能系统中，大模型主要负责认知层，包括任务理解、场景理解和 
高层规划，控制层则结合模仿学习、强化学习与传统运动控制算法形成行动链；券商报告简介表示其采用 G1–G5 具身智能技术分级体系，并判断当前技术普遍处于 G2 阶段向 G3     
演进。[19][20]                                                                                                                                                   

现有公开资料显示：报告简介称内容包括具身智能技术体系结构分析和对代表性人形机器人公司产品现状与技术路径的研究；北京人形机器人创新中心的《具身智能发展报告》明确目 
标是从 AI                                                                                                                                                        
视角厘清具身智能概念、演进历程和技术体系，梳理技术发展现状并分析应用潜力与影响；报告摘要指出其技术架构包括感知、认知和控制的一体化设计，并对具身智能体进行分级， 
分析关键技术；报告摘要提到其综述国内外代表性公司和项目，可能包括 OpenAI 相关具身智能项目以及 Figure 和 1X 等人形机器人公司。[20][21]                             

现有公开资料显示：Many embodied intelligence and humanoid robot systems adopt a general architecture in which visual and language models handle perception and   
task understanding, a behavior‑planning module generates action plans, and low‑level control uses a combination of imitation learning, reinforcement learning,   
and traditional motion control to execute actions in a closed loop.；Analysts and research reports commonly describe humanoid robot technology stacks as         
comprising four layers: mechanics and actuation, perception and environment modeling, decision‑making and control, and an embodied intelligence layer integrating
perception, cognition, and control.；Industry analyses distinguish two main technical routes for embodied intelligence: (1) a large‑model‑centric route in which 
general cognition via foundation models is combined with learning‑based control, exemplified by OpenAI‑invested companies such as Figure; and (2) a route led by 
traditional robot control and engineering rules with gradually added learning modules, used by some industrial robot firms.；Figure AI’s Figure 01 humanoid robot
follows a technical path in which visual and audio perception are processed by generative AI and large language models for task and scene understanding and      
high‑level planning, while mid‑tier control performs task decomposition and action‑sequence planning and low‑tier joint control relies on traditional robotics,  
imitation learning, and reinforcement learning to execute grasping and device manipulation.。[18][19][15][21][17][13][14]                                        

现有公开资料显示：Figure AI uses OpenAI’s generative and large language models for high‑level cognition in Figure 01, including natural‑language instruction     
parsing and visual scene understanding, under a strategic cooperation where Figure provides embodied deployment scenarios and OpenAI provides model              
capabilities.；Figure 01 is positioned as a general‑purpose humanoid "universal workforce" robot targeted at warehouse, manufacturing, and service scenarios, and
in 2024 it conducted pilot demonstrations in warehouse and factory automation with large enterprises, but remained in a trial rather than mass‑production        
stage.；Figure AI’s January 5, 2024 demonstration video shows Figure 01 using a generative‑AI‑based control pipeline to interpret language instructions and      
perform a sequence of grasping and operating actions to place a capsule in a coffee machine and make coffee, illustrating its claimed end‑to‑end                 
language‑to‑action control route.；Figure AI received multiple rounds of high‑value financing, including a major round around February 25, 2024 involving OpenAI 
as an investor, leading to a valuation exceeding approximately 2.6 billion USD despite being less than two years old, and is frequently described as a star      
company in the embodied intelligence and humanoid robot domain.。[13][14][15][18]                                                                                

现有公开资料显示：1X Technologies focuses its product roadmap on embodied security robots and humanoid‑form robots, primarily for security, monitoring, guarding,
and patrolling scenarios, and emphasizes safety and stability more strongly in its control strategy than some other general‑purpose humanoid robot firms.；1X    
Technologies applies a data‑driven control strategy that combines visual perception with large‑model‑based decision‑making to control its security robots,       
aligning with OpenAI’s vision of bringing general AI models into the physical world.；By 2024, 1X’s humanoid security robots had entered testing and early       
commercial deployment, while Tesla’s Optimus was in internal factory trial operation and Figure 01 was conducting pilot demonstrations in warehouse and          
manufacturing scenarios, indicating that representative embodied‑intelligence humanoid systems were in prototype and limited deployment stages rather than broad 
commercialization.；OpenAI provides both investment and technical model support to embodied‑intelligence and humanoid‑robot companies such as Figure AI and 1X   
Technologies, including leading a 23.5 million USD A2 round for 1X in March 2023 and contributing models within a later major financing and strategic            
collaboration with Figure.。[13][18][15][17][14]                                                                                                                 

现有公开资料显示：Analyst and industry articles in 2024–2025 regard Figure AI, 1X Technologies, and Tesla as representative companies in the general‑purpose     
humanoid robot track, with Figure and 1X highlighted as core players that have received funding at the hundreds‑of‑millions‑of‑USD level amid a broader surge in 
embodied‑intelligence financing.；Several research and market reports published for 2024–2025 focus explicitly on embodied intelligence and humanoid robots,     
analyzing technical architectures, grading embodied‑intelligence systems (e.g., G1–G5 levels, with most systems assessed at G2 moving toward G3 by late 2024),   
and reviewing product status, technical routes, iteration plans, and supply‑chain structures of representative companies likely including OpenAI‑related         
projects, Figure, and 1X.；Industry timelines for the humanoid‑robot and embodied‑intelligence sector often characterize 2024 as a prototype or "original        
machine" year, 2025 as the beginning of mass production, and 2026 as the anticipated commercialization boom year, with some commentators expecting 2026 to be    
widely viewed as the start of large‑scale commercial deployment and the appearance of humanoid products priced as low as 99,000 RMB.；Industry commentary around 
2026 suggests that technical routes for embodied intelligence are shifting from single‑model‑driven systems toward approaches centered on data, simulation, and  
toolchains, stressing the importance of data collection, high‑quality simulators, and integrated learning infrastructures.。[15][18][16][20][21][17]             

现有公开资料显示：Founding teams of leading embodied‑intelligence and humanoid‑robot companies, including Figure AI, commonly draw talent from major technology  
firms such as Tesla, Apple, and Google, and from domains including robotics, autonomous driving, and AI, reflecting a cross‑disciplinary background pattern in   
this sector.。[14][18]                                                                                                                                           

